# what the linked compiler frontend needs from the thread it runs on
#
# mls compiles the compiler's own frontend into itself and runs it on the
# analysis thread and the rebuild worker. The compiler runs that frontend on a
# thread it sizes itself, and its readers refuse an input by the stack left, so
# how deep a project may nest follows the reserve. A thread spawned with std's
# 2 MiB default, or any reserve below the compiler's, refuses in mls what mach
# builds (#345). A reserve is address space, not memory, so holding the
# compiler's own size costs nothing until the frontend actually uses it.

use lstack: mach.lang.stack;
use std.types.size.usize;

# the stack reserve of every thread that runs the linked frontend, in bytes
pub val STACK_RESERVE: usize = lstack.WORKER_RESERVE;
